title the room folds, and two numbers meet
prompt Keaton gave the word on the session-logs fold -- the one the rule holds for his hand.
think The mark law says no fold ships without dated_path_witness GREEN, so ran it before touching anything. It was RED: 191 lost references against a ceiling of 187. Standfast before the fold.
think All four arrivals came from rounds explaining themselves well. Two reproduced REDS %202's fabricated path -- in the ledger row describing it and in the log narrating it. One was a name planted by the commit-msg control. One was a log naming a sibling that was never written.
think The mark law had already booked this shape and named three fabrications on the day it was written. It fired again inside the guard written to prevent it, which is the sharpest form it has taken.
think Repaired what could be repaired and left what could not. The ledger row names the stamp rather than reproducing the path; the planted control name joined DP_FIXTURE_BASENAMES, the seated mechanism for a name built to match nothing; two session logs keep every word they wrote.
think Then went looking for genuine repairs rather than raising the ceiling, and found the same recalled-stamp fault standing in the tree before this round made its own: gratitude/toyota-production-system.md cited 20260729-222500 twice where the tree carries 224828. And context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md carried a citation the Sala -> Seva rename had swept while the dated filename it names correctly never followed.
obs The fold is correct by the law's own test. 169 logs moved, recoverable references rose 9,070 -> 9,246, and lost held at 186 -- a fold changes paths and keeps basenames, so a correct one leaves the lost count where it stood. Ceiling lowered 187 -> 186 on the repair.
obs 3,415 shelf links across 33 shelves, none broken. The pin fell 291,781 -> 29,997 bytes, a 90% reduction, and the front door came out correct without a hand: title at the top, rows under the delimiter, newest first.
obs And it is still 5,421 bytes over the bound it declares. The prose takes 2,033, leaving 22,543 for rows that average 798, so the pin holds about 28 and today made 35. The law says the byte bound follows from folding; measured, it does not on a working day. Booked as REDS %204 with the choice surfaced rather than made.
obs declared_ceiling ratchets pages-over as a COUNT, so it read 1 before a 90% fall and 1 after. A count of pages cannot see a page improve, which is worth knowing about the meter as well as the page.
loom fold room=session-logs moved=169 flat_after=36 date_rooms=61 shelves=33 shelf_links=3415 broken=0
loom pin bytes_before=291781 bytes_after=29997 bound=24576 over=5421 rows=35 avg_row_bytes=798
loom census lost_before=191 lost_after=186 ceiling=187->186 recoverable=9070->9246
